1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:12,000
Section 1 You will hear a woman telephoning a tourist office to ask about free activities.

2
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:29,063
First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 6.

3
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:52,640
[silence] You will see that there is an example that has been done for you.

4
00:00:52,721 --> 00:00:59,040
On this occasion only, the conversation relating to this will be played first.

5
00:00:59,119 --> 00:01:03,998
Good morning, this is Burnham Tourist Office, Martin speaking.

6
00:01:04,076 --> 00:01:04,863
Oh, hello.

7
00:01:04,942 --> 00:01:12,829
I saw a poster about three things to do in the area, and it said people should phone you for information.

8
00:01:12,894 --> 00:01:21,004
I'm coming to Burnham with my husband and two children for a few days on June the 27th, or possibly the 28th,

9
00:01:21,004 --> 00:01:25,067
and I'd like some ideas for things to do on the 29th.

10
00:01:25,085 --> 00:01:26,000
I'd like some ideas for things to do on the 29th.

11
00:01:26,133 --> 00:01:30,000
Yes of course.

12
00:01:30,097 --> 00:01:40,000
The date that the woman wants information about is the 29th of June, so the letter C has been circled.

13
00:01:40,081 --> 00:01:41,617
Now we shall begin.

14
00:01:41,698 --> 00:01:50,966
You should answer the questions as you listen because you will not hear the recording a second time.

15
00:01:51,088 --> 00:01:56,560
Listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 6.

16
00:01:56,657 --> 00:02:02,560
Good morning, this is Burnham Tourist Office Martin speaking.

17
00:02:02,631 --> 00:02:10,800
Oh hello, I saw a poster about free things to do in the area and it said people should phone you for information.

18
00:02:10,879 --> 00:02:23,680
I'm coming to Burnham with my husband and two children for a few days on June 27th or possibly the 28th and I'd like some ideas for things to do on the 29th.

19
00:02:23,789 --> 00:02:25,309
Yes of course.

20
00:02:25,417 --> 00:02:25,960
Okay.

21
00:02:26,011 --> 00:02:29,320
Then let's start with a couple of events especially for children.

22
00:02:29,374 --> 00:02:36,520
The Art Gallery is holding an event called Family Welcome that day when there are activities and trails to use throughout the gallery.

23
00:02:36,585 --> 00:02:38,140
That sounds interesting.

24
00:02:38,205 --> 00:02:39,760
What time does it start?

25
00:02:39,824 --> 00:02:45,240
The gallery opens at 10 and the Family Welcome event runs from 10.30 until 2 o'clock.

26
00:02:45,294 --> 00:02:52,880
The gallery stays open until 5 and several times during the day they're going to show a short film that the gallery has produced.

27
00:02:52,929 --> 00:02:59,400
It demonstrates how ceramics are made and there'll be equipment and materials for children to have a go themselves.

28
00:02:59,444 --> 00:03:06,360
Last time they ran the event there was a film about painting which went down very well with the children and they're now working on one about sculpture.

29
00:03:06,447 --> 00:03:12,120
I like the sound of that and what other events happen in Burnham.

30
00:03:12,168 --> 00:03:14,120
Well do you all enjoy listening to music?

31
00:03:14,245 --> 00:03:15,120
Oh yes.

32
00:03:15,179 --> 00:03:20,880
Well there are several free concerts taking place at different times, one or two in the morning,

33
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:26,000
the majority at lunchtime and a couple in the evening and they range from pop music to Latin American.

34
00:03:26,077 --> 00:03:30,000
The Latin American could be fun, what time is that?

35
00:03:30,054 --> 00:03:32,893
It's been repeated several times in different places.

36
00:03:32,946 --> 00:03:38,171
They're performing in the central library at one o'clock, then at four it's in the city museum,

37
00:03:38,171 --> 00:03:42,000
and in the evening at 730 there's a longer concert in the theatre.

38
00:03:42,079 --> 00:03:46,120
Right, I'll suggest that to the rest of the family.

39
00:03:46,166 --> 00:03:49,640
Something else you might be interested in is the boat race along the river.

40
00:03:49,715 --> 00:03:52,280
Oh yes, do you tell me about that?

41
00:03:52,343 --> 00:03:57,960
The race starts at offered Marina to the north of Burnham and goes as far as Summer Pool.

42
00:03:58,011 --> 00:04:02,720
The best place to watch it from is Charles Worth Bridge, though that does get rather crowded.

43
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:04,320
And who's taking part?

44
00:04:04,370 --> 00:04:07,000
Well local boat clubs, but the standard is very high.

45
00:04:07,058 --> 00:04:12,000
One of them came first in the West of England Regional Championship in May this year.

46
00:04:12,063 --> 00:04:15,000
It was the first time a team from Burnhamers 1.

47
00:04:15,056 --> 00:04:23,000
It means that next year they'll be representing the region in the National Championship.

48
00:04:23,385 --> 00:04:58,400
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 7-10.

49
00:04:58,471 --> 00:05:02,240
Now I've heard something about Paxton Nature Reserve.

50
00:05:02,289 --> 00:05:05,000
It's a good place for spotting unusual birds, isn't it?

51
00:05:05,057 --> 00:05:07,000
That's right, throughout the year.

52
00:05:07,058 --> 00:05:12,000
There is a lake there as well as a river, and they provide a very attractive habitat.

53
00:05:12,052 --> 00:05:15,000
So it's a good idea to bring binoculars if you have them.

54
00:05:15,053 --> 00:05:19,000
And just at the moment you can see various flowers that are pretty unusual.

55
00:05:19,053 --> 00:05:21,000
The soil at Paxton isn't very common.

56
00:05:21,063 --> 00:05:23,000
They're looking good right now.

57
00:05:23,077 --> 00:05:23,536
Right!

58
00:05:23,613 --> 00:05:27,520
My husband will be particularly interested in that.

59
00:05:27,575 --> 00:05:31,040
And there's going to be a talk and a slideshow about mushrooms,

60
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:35,200
and you'll be able to go out and pick some afterwards and study the different varieties.

61
00:05:35,265 --> 00:05:35,716
Uh-huh.

62
00:05:35,781 --> 00:05:39,200
And is it possible for children to swim in the river?

63
00:05:39,251 --> 00:05:39,455
Yes.

64
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:43,120
Part of it has been fenced off to make it safe for children to swim in.

65
00:05:43,173 --> 00:05:46,891
It's very shallow, and there's a lifeguard on duty whenever it's open.

66
00:05:46,944 --> 00:05:50,440
The lake is too deep, so swimming isn't allowed there.

67
00:05:50,504 --> 00:05:55,347
OK, we must remember to bring their swimming things in case we go to Paxton.

68
00:05:55,410 --> 00:05:59,520
How long does it take to get there by car from Burnham?

69
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:06,814
About 20 minutes, but parking is very limited, so it's usually much easier to go by bus, and it takes about the same time.

70
00:06:06,872 --> 00:06:07,221
Right.

71
00:06:07,279 --> 00:06:11,161
Well, I'll discuss the options with the rest of the family.

72
00:06:11,276 --> 00:06:15,306
Thanks very much for all your help.

73
00:06:15,421 --> 00:06:17,148
You're welcome.

74
00:06:17,263 --> 00:06:18,184
Goodbye.

75
00:06:18,299 --> 00:06:18,760
Bye.

76
00:06:19,146 --> 00:06:30,352
That is the end of section 1.

77
00:06:30,739 --> 00:06:49,673
You now have half a minute to check your answers.

78
00:06:50,059 --> 00:06:58,560
Now turn to section 2.